                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Unfortunately, there are just too many issues with the game, I can't recommend it.\n\nThere are glitches where both workers and orders get stuck.  This happened three times during my short time with the game.  With workers, you fire the stuck character and then re-hire a worker of the same type.  Unfortunately, when you do this, you lose any money invested in training the fired/glitchy worker.\n\nMy store didn't have a lot of lights or other hot items, yet it was very difficult to get the heat down in the store to an acceptable level.  I had to install 10 A/C vents just to get the store temperature under 24 degrees celsius.\n\nIt takes the workers a long time to build and install bought parts in the store.  This really slows down the gameplay.\n\nIt is lacking the marketing aspect of owning a store.  I think being able to promote your business would have really added to the gameplay.\n\nThe graphics are fine for the game.  I didn't feel as though the praphics held the gameplay back.\nThere are other aspects of the game that did hold it back and made the game unenjoyable, such as stuck workers, A/C and no marketing.  They are the reason why I can't recommend the game.\n\nI think it could be a good game with some minor improvements.",
